<title>POLAND: Most Polish min T-bill prices rise at tender.</title>
<headline>Most Polish min T-bill prices rise at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills rose at today's primary auction on total demand of 1.978 billion zlotys against a 700 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold its entire 700 million zloty offer.  </p>
<p>			 8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	95.48    91.13     --	83.54</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.45)  (91.11)    --     (83.53)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.72    91.53     --	83.81</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.70)  (91.18)    --     (84.15)</p>
<p>   offer		--	150.0    100.0     --	450.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	564.0    450.3     --	963.3</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	150.0    100.0     --	450.0</p>
<p>   next auction     --	100.0    100.0     --	400.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
